== 3.7 Chapter 3 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The law of supply states that, other things being equal,],
  [price and quantity supplied move in the same direction],
  [quantity supplied is fixed in the short run],
  [price and quantity supplied move in opposite directions],
  [supply rises when demand falls]
)

#mcq(2, [The supply curve of a commodity slopes upward because],
  [costs fall as output rises],
  [the government requires it],
  [producers offer more at higher prices],
  [consumers buy less at higher prices]
)

#mcq(3, [Supply in economics means the quantity of a good that sellers],
  [would like to sell at any price at all],
  [have already sold],
  [are willing and able to offer at each price over a period],
  [have in stock at the end of the year]
)

#mcq(4, [A movement along a supply curve is caused by a change in],
  [technology],
  [the number of sellers],
  [the cost of raw materials],
  [the price of the good itself]
)

#mcq(5, [A rise in the cost of raw materials will shift the supply curve],
  [to the right],
  [to the left],
  [not at all],
  [along itself]
)

#mcq(6, [An improvement in technology will shift the supply curve],
  [to a vertical position],
  [to the left],
  [along itself],
  [to the right]
)

#mcq(7, [A subsidy paid to producers will],
  [shift supply to the left],
  [shift demand to the right],
  [have no effect on supply],
  [shift supply to the right]
)

#mcq(8, [An increase in the number of sellers in a market will],
  [shift demand to the right],
  [shift supply to the right],
  [shift supply to the left],
